USE [OPERATIONSTOOL]
GO

/*
    Transport Performance Dashboard.

    One row per IMCD pick (latest carrier import of that number).
    A carrier value such as 03344463-OUT matches pick 3344463.
    Fecha Entrega is Carrier_Imported_Data.Delivery_Date, from the carrier file.
    The period filter and the monthly chart use the promised delivery date.
    The pick is late when that date is after the later of the promised
    delivery date and the earliest viable date, or when the order has a
    Cases row with CASE_ATTRIBUTED = 'Delivery Timing'.

    Earliest viable date = warehouse arrival date + TransitTime.Transit_Days.
    Warehouse arrival date is the earliest EDI_DATETIME for the order where
    SOURCE = 'Inbound Messages'. A time after 13:30 moves that date to the
    next working day (Saturday and Sunday roll to Monday). Holidays are not
    applied in this version.

    The on-time target is CFG_CarrierTargetPercentage in
    dbo.ConfigurationOperationsTool.

    Procedures:
      AccountOwners_Consult, Zones_Consult, Product_Search, Account_Search
        Lookup lists for the filter bar.
      Consult
        Dashboard. Three result sets from one filtered set:
        1 summary row, one row per month, then the current page of picks.
        @pickNumber and @orderNumber are the last parameters so an older
        caller that does not pass them still lines up.
      Unmatched_Consult
        Carrier picks that do not match a sales-budget pick. Two result sets:
        the count, then the page. @pickNumber is the last parameter.
      Pick_Consult
        One pick for the details page. Five result sets: header, sales lines,
        every carrier row, EDI messages, Delivery Timing cases.
*/

